# AArch64 port of upstream's Nix packaging.
#
# Purely a record for review: the fork is applied by being committed under
# nix/, not by being patched at flake evaluation time. Nix cannot apply a patch
# during a pure evaluation, so the vendored copy is the mechanism and this file
# is the description of what changed.
#
# Regenerate with tools/regenerate-nix-fork, which re-extracts upstream nix/ and
# re-applies it. The CI check does the same and fails on any difference.
#
# Upstream v0.5.0, commit c56aa2d6e8d70bd87b279e4edd70588c7ec15a6d.
#
# Three groups of change:
#   1. denialSource, because the fork no longer sits beside upstream's tree, so
#      ../prebuilt, ../compositor and ../native_app are passed in as an argument
#      instead. overlay.nix publishes it as a package set attribute, which is
#      how callPackage hands it to every file that declares it.
#   2. The dart and engine source hash tables gain an aarch64-linux key, and the
#      Dart archive name follows the target. Upstream keys these by system with
#      a throw as the fallback, so packages.aarch64-linux did not exist rather
#      than failing to build.
#   3. meta.platforms gains aarch64-linux. These are enforced on derivations
#      built by callPackage inside package.nix's own let, which was confirmed on
#      an AArch64 runner rather than assumed.

